</h1><p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground">Tariffs, customs rulings, intermodal practice, and what it all means for the cargo on your docks.</p></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 lg:px-10 pb-28"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6"><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/supply-chain-disruptions-freight-planning" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/supply-chain-disruptions-freight-planning-DSuSQF_G.jpg" alt="A blank &quot;PLAN&quot; list note pinned to a corkboard" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Supply Chain</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">Supply Chain Disruptions: How to Build a Freight Plan That Holds Up</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">Every importer has a disruption story. The disruption itself rarely costs the most — it&#x27;s the scramble to find someone who can actually do something about it that does.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">July 17, 2026</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/construction-equipment-tariffs-2026" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/construction-equipment-tariffs-2026-BisJ_tMi.jpg" alt="Aerial view of excavators, dump trucks, and a bulldozer parked at a construction site" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Tariffs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">Section 232 Construction Equipment Tariffs Just Got More Complicated for Importers. Here&#x27;s What Actually Changed.</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">Section 232 duties on construction equipment, forklifts, and mobile industrial machinery changed again on June 1, 2026. The headlines focus on rate cuts, but eligibility depends on origin, classification, and metal content.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">June 29, 2026</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/freight-visibility-tracking-blue-ridge" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/freight-visibility-tracking-blue-ridge-CfDYp82D.jpg" alt="A warehouse team reviewing shipment data on a laptop among stacked boxes" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Technology</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">You Shouldn&#x27;t Have to Chase Your Own Cargo — How Freight Visibility Tracking Elevates Your Business</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">International freight is already complicated. Figuring out where your shipment is — and what &#x27;in transit&#x27; actually means right now — shouldn&#x27;t add to that.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">May 22, 2026</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/section-232-annex-iii-2026-updates" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/section-232-annex-iii-2026-updates-B_O5aLQX.jpg" alt="A person calculating figures on a calculator beside a laptop displaying charts" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Tariffs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">Section 232 Just Changed the Math. Here&#x27;s What Annex III Means for Your Imports.</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">A new presidential proclamation restructured Section 232 tariffs on steel, aluminum, and copper effective April 6, 2026 — and for a narrow category of industrial equipment, Annex III opens a temporary window of relief before it closes at the end of 2027.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">April 8, 2026</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/us-import-duties-update" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/us-import-duties-update-DYr7_vRH.jpg" alt="A calculator displaying the word FEES surrounded by stacks of coins and cash" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Trade Policy</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">What&#x27;s Happening with U.S. Duties Right Now — And What It Actually Means for Your Cargo</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">If you&#x27;re importing chemicals, machinery, or high-value goods right now, the noise around U.S. import duties, tariffs, and trade policy isn&#x27;t abstract. It&#x27;s a line item.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">March 23, 2026</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/ieepa-tariffs-ruled-unlawful" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/ieepa-tariffs-ruled-unlawful-DkMfGjh_.jpg" alt="A judge&#x27;s gavel resting on its sound block" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Tariffs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">The Supreme Court Just Ruled IEEPA Tariffs Were Unlawful. Here&#x27;s What That Means for Your Imports</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">In Learning Resources, Inc. v. Trump, the Supreme Court ruled 6-3 that the president lacked authority under IEEPA to impose tariffs. If your business paid IEEPA duties, you may be entitled to a refund — but the clock is already ticking.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">February 20, 2026</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/best-practices-inland-drayage-rail-intermodal" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/best-practices-inland-drayage-rail-intermodal-Cyyi2KLP.jpg" alt="A straddle crane lifts and stacks containers in a port" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Drayage</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">Best Practices for Inland Drayage and Rail-Intermodal Integration in the U.S. Supply Chain</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">Smooth intermodal integration between rail and truck transport is critical for an efficient, sustainable U.S. supply chain. The first and last miles often determine whether a shipment succeeds.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">December 18, 2025</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/transloading-services-cost-speed" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/transloading-services-cost-speed-DjmQdWzk.jpg" alt="A forklift removes a pallet from a truck" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Transloading</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">The Role of Transloading &amp; CFS Services in Reducing Cargo Costs and Improving Speed</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">Competent shippers are turning to transloading and CFS services to keep cargo moving quickly and affordably as regulations shift. Here&#x27;s how these services cut costs and time.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">December 8, 2025</div></div></a></div><div style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)"><a href="/news/complete-freight-flow" class="group flex flex-col h-full rounded-2xl bg-surface overflow-hidden hover:bg-muted transition-colors"><div class="overflow-hidden"><img src="/assets/complete-freight-flow-BCFHbDpR.jpg" alt="Stacked shipping containers on a cargo vessel at port" class="w-full h-44 object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 p-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber">Operations</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></div><h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance">The Complete Freight Flow: How Blue Ridge Orchestrates from Port to Inland Delivery</h2><p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm flex-1">From port to final inland delivery, every handoff, document, and schedule matters. We’ve built a freight flow that puts visibility, communication, and coordination at the center.</p><div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">November 26, 2025</div></div></a></div></div><nav aria-label="News pagination" class="mt-16 flex items-center justify-between gap-4"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground/30"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-left h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path></svg>Previous</span><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><a class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground font-mono text-xs active" href="/news" data-status="active" aria-current="page">1</a><a href="/news/page/2" class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground hover:bg-muted transition-colors font-mono text-xs">2</a></div><a href="/news/page/2" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Next<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" wid